WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:04.691
Speaker 1: All right, today we're going to
start by looking at how many of his 100 day

00:00:04.691 --> 00:00:10.980
promises Joe Biden has accomplished as president,
either partially or fully. And I think it

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:17.440
makes sense to say at the outset that we will
evaluate whether he did the things he promised

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:23.340
to do. The the question of whether he promised
to do the right things is a separate one.

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:28.160
So, like as an example, if Joe Biden promised
to cancel ten thousand dollars in student

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:33.110
debt and did it, but you think he should have
done 50 thousand, these are two different

00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:37.220
questions that he promised the right thing
and that he achieved the thing that he promised.

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:43.350
But let's just jump right into it, starting
with climate. The NPR and the AP have really

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:48.400
good trackers on this. And I encourage you
to check out I'm looking at the Associated

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:54.290
Press tracker and it's very, very good. So
on climate for promises Joe Biden has kept,

00:00:54.290 --> 00:00:59.510
he has taken executive action to reduce greenhouse
gas emissions. He did rejoin the Paris climate

00:00:59.510 --> 00:01:06.810
accord. He supported an amendment to the Montreal
Protocol to curb H.F. Seas. And he has convened

00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:11.770
a world climate summit which recently took
place. He did those four things that he promised.

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:19.220
He has not yet done infrastructure that will
sort of be done in a way that takes into account

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:24.409
the big picture climate picture. He just hasn't
done infrastructure yet. He has not taken

00:01:24.409 --> 00:01:29.960
steps to conserve, conserve 30 percent of
U.S. lands and waters by 2030. And he has

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:35.420
not received emission reductions commitments
from the shipping and aviation industry on

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:40.720
the economy. Joe Biden has accomplished four
of his five promises. He has extended a pause

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:47.280
on student loan payments. He did pandemic
relief one point nine trillion. He did review

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:52.721
the US supply chain for vulnerabilities in
key sectors. Those have been identified. He

00:01:52.721 --> 00:01:57.840
has taken steps to strengthen by American
measures, and he has not yet increased the

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:02.640
corporate tax rate. So four out of five on
economy and taxes. Now, you might be saying,

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:06.840
well, hold on, he made other promises economically.
Yes, but they were not hundred day promises.

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:12.591
We're looking at 100 day promises on government
functioning. He has done three or four. He

00:02:12.591 --> 00:02:18.660
tightened ethics rules. He insulated the Justice
Department from politics. He eased federal

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:24.810
unionization restrictions. He did not restore
rules that were weakened by Donald Trump on

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:30.819
gun control. He's really done nothing yet.
He promised to send Congress a gun control

00:02:30.819 --> 00:02:37.690
bill. It's sort of partially been met, but
it's not been completed. He promised to reauthorize

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:44.170
the Violence Against Women Act. It's on its
way, but it has not yet been done commissioning

00:02:44.170 --> 00:02:49.520
an attorney general report to restructure
agencies to enforce gun laws he's gotten.

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:56.790
Merrick Garland started on it, but it's not
yet been done. And he also promised an FBI

00:02:56.790 --> 00:03:02.281
report on how to tighten gun purchase. Background
check loopholes has not been done. Health

00:03:02.281 --> 00:03:07.420
care. He made eight promises for his first
hundred days and he's done five. He did do

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:13.200
a massive mandate on federal property. He
rejoined the World Health Organization. He

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:17.980
set up one hundred mass vaccination centers.
He vaccinated one hundred million Americans,

00:03:17.980 --> 00:03:22.569
actually two hundred million. And he did deploy
mobile vaccination clinics. He has not expanded

00:03:22.569 --> 00:03:28.840
health care access in a meaningful way yet,
and he has not outlined new pandemic measures

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:33.281
for future pandemics that's been requested.
It's sort of, you could say, in process. And

00:03:33.281 --> 00:03:38.069
he has not yet reopened most elementary and
middle schools on housing. He said he would

00:03:38.069 --> 00:03:43.140
pause evictions and foreclosures, and he did.
And there were some other strategic things

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:47.650
like coming up with a strategy to make housing
a right that's not yet been done. So he did

00:03:47.650 --> 00:03:52.299
do one thing on housing. Immigration is a
tough one. There were a lot of immigration

00:03:52.299 --> 00:03:57.909
promises made. In fact, seventeen many have
not been accomplished. The naturalization

00:03:57.909 --> 00:04:04.720
process hasn't been streamlined. Increases
to the amount of refugees have not taken place.

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:10.850
But he did send Congress an immigration bill,
which he promised to do. He did revise deportation

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:14.310
criteria, although many people would say,
yeah, they were revised, but it's not nearly

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:21.060
enough. He did take steps to reunite separated
migrant families. He did end the travel ban.

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:26.610
He did stop deportations for certain groups.
And with a lot of these with the immigration

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:32.569
stuff, the devil is really in the details
where the promise is very open ended. So you

00:04:32.569 --> 00:04:36.889
and I would look at what's going on with deportations
and we would say there's still a ton of them

00:04:36.889 --> 00:04:44.550
going on. The promise was to stop deportations
for certain groups and he did sign a memo

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:50.789
on that. But we I don't feel it's nearly enough.
He stopped border wall construction, reversed

00:04:50.789 --> 00:04:54.229
the public charge rule for immigrants. And
then there's a whole bunch of other stuff

00:04:54.229 --> 00:04:59.419
that is sort of arguably in progress he's
asked for. It hasn't really happened. He.

00:04:59.419 --> 00:05:03.419
Promised to freeze deportations for 100 days.
Remember, he did it, but then it was blocked

00:05:03.419 --> 00:05:10.850
by a judge on inequality. Basically nothing
has yet been done. He made 12 promises. The

00:05:10.850 --> 00:05:17.139
only one that's been accomplished is creating
a a working group, a union issues working

00:05:17.139 --> 00:05:22.120
group to deliver a plan on increasing union
membership that's been done. All the other

00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:27.159
stuff hasn't, you know, addressing systemic
racism in U.S. institutions, signing the Equality

00:05:27.159 --> 00:05:31.270
Act, appointing a commission to study sexual
assault in the military. These are things

00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:36.460
that Joe Biden has said he wants done while
being president. So so they're marked as in

00:05:36.460 --> 00:05:42.630
process. They have not yet been done. And
then on national security, Joe Biden promised

00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:47.810
to rejoin the Iran nuclear deal. He has he
has started that process. It has not happened.

00:05:47.810 --> 00:05:53.059
So how do you grade his promises? I mean,
you know, the thing that's tough about this

00:05:53.059 --> 00:05:58.279
is a lot of these promises we all knew were
never going to happen, much like with Trump.

00:05:58.279 --> 00:06:02.719
We knew where Trump was, never going to build
a wall across the entire border and get Mexico

00:06:02.719 --> 00:06:07.060
to pay for it in his first four years. This
was never going to happen. And he failed.

00:06:07.060 --> 00:06:12.369
And so it was a promise he failed to deliver
on. Trump was never going to pay off the national

00:06:12.369 --> 00:06:17.490
debt in four years. And of course, he blew
it up. Actually, Joe Biden's promises were

00:06:17.490 --> 00:06:23.309
more reasonable, but some were still clearly
not going to happen. So if we just grade him

00:06:23.309 --> 00:06:31.809
on a percentage basis, it's like a C, if we
grade him based on his intentions via things

00:06:31.809 --> 00:06:38.240
he signed orders on, but obviously take longer
than 100 days. And we account for all of the

00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:45.949
realities. It's probably like a B plus. But
but with all of these things, the questions

00:06:45.949 --> 00:06:53.990
really are how do we interpret his intention
to do something versus the practicality? When

00:06:53.990 --> 00:06:58.819
you understand that there are other players
involved, you're going to have to tell me

00:06:58.819 --> 00:07:03.699
how how to evaluate that. And ultimately,
voters are going to decide some great things

00:07:03.699 --> 00:07:09.189
done. And compared to many other presidents,
this has been one of the most productive first

00:07:09.189 --> 00:07:15.399
100 days compared to all the things he promised.
If you just you don't do a curve of any kind

00:07:15.399 --> 00:07:20.409
that accounts for practical difficulties,
it's like he's done kind of, you know, half

00:07:20.409 --> 00:07:25.069
the stuff or something like that. So let me
know your thoughts on how we should be evaluating

00:07:25.069 --> 00:07:35.429
it. I

